CommitProof mutant M2 — cohort-add-local-view (CONTRACT §9.2, ADR-0007)

Intent: in MultipoolerManager.UpdateConsensusRule
(go/services/multipooler/internal/manager/rpc_manager.go:405), for
RULE_OPERATION_COHORT_ADD only, apply the incoming synchronous-standby policy
(the new member is counted for acks) and return success without writing the
rule (DoUpdateRule skipped). Every other operation is unchanged.
Failure mode modelled: membership admitted from a local view instead of by
consensus — a write acknowledged with the new member's participation is lost
when a failover recruits from the old cohort (S41's 3→4 scenario; the leader-
led ADD path of S24).
Sources: S41, S24.
Detection (§9.2): directed schedule D2; expected C1 lost-write.
Function touched: UpdateConsensusRule (one function).

